11
00:57:45,000 --> 00:57:51,000
High Plains Drifter is a 1973 American Western film directed by Clint Eastwood, written by Ernest
Tidyman, and produced by Robert Daley for The Malpaso Company and Universal Pictures.

12
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
The film stars Eastwood as a mysterious stranger who metes
out justice in a corrupt frontier mining town.

13
01:08:15,000 --> 01:08:21,000
The film was influenced by the work of Eastwood's collaborators,
the film directors Sergio Leone and Don Siegel.

14
01:13:30,000 --> 01:13:36,000
The film co-stars Verna Bloom, Mariana Hill, Mitchell
Ryan, Jack Ging and Stefan Gierasch.

15
01:18:45,000 --> 01:18:51,000
The film was shot on location on the southern shores of Mono Lake, California.

16
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
Dee Barton wrote the film score.

17
01:29:15,000 --> 01:29:21,000
The film was critically acclaimed at the time of its
initial release and remains popular.

18
